Date: Fri, 16 Oct 2026 21:23:53 +0700
Subject: [PATCH 38/38] Present the sheets and alerts of hosting views that are
 not a window's root through UIKit

A UIHostingController that is a child of another view controller, or the
view controller of a representable, presents its content's sheets, covers,
alerts and confirmation dialogs with UIKit's present, each in a hosting
controller of its own over the whole window, as SwiftUI does on iOS. The
window's root hosting controller shows them over its content as before;
menus stay there too, as they place themselves in the content's
coordinates. A representable's view controller hears appearance callbacks
from UIKit as its view comes and goes.
